public static class ObjectInfo {
 public static double? Number(string value){double n;return double.TryParse(value,NumberStyles.Float,CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,out n)&&!double.IsNaN(n)&&!double.IsInfinity(n)?(double?)n:null;}
 public static void Merge(Target to,Target from){to.Vmag=to.Vmag??from.Vmag;to.Bmag=to.Bmag??from.Bmag;to.Jmag=to.Jmag??from.Jmag;to.Hmag=to.Hmag??from.Hmag;to.Kmag=to.Kmag??from.Kmag;to.SurfaceBrightness=to.SurfaceBrightness??from.SurfaceBrightness;if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(to.MagnitudeBand))to.MagnitudeBand=from.MagnitudeBand;if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(to.Constellation))to.Constellation=from.Constellation;if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(to.Morphology))to.Morphology=from.Morphology;if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(to.CatalogNotes))to.CatalogNotes=from.CatalogNotes;}
 public static string RA(double ra){int s=(int)Math.Round(ra*3600)%86400;return (s/3600).ToString("00")+"h "+(s/60%60).ToString("00")+"m "+(s%60).ToString("00")+"s";}
 public static string Dec(double dec){int s=(int)Math.Round(Math.Abs(dec)*3600);return (dec<0?"−":"+")+(s/3600).ToString("00")+"° "+(s/60%60).ToString("00")+"′ "+(s%60).ToString("00")+"″";}
 public static string Coordinates(Pick pick,Night night){var eq=pick.Target.Body.HasValue?night.Coords(pick.Target,pick.Best):default(Equatorial);return "RA "+RA(pick.Target.Body.HasValue?eq.ra:pick.Target.Ra)+" · Dec "+Dec(pick.Target.Body.HasValue?eq.dec:pick.Target.Dec)+(pick.Target.Body.HasValue?" (of date, at best)":" (J2000)");}
 static string M(double? value){return value.HasValue?value.Value.ToString("0.00",CultureInfo.InvariantCulture):"not cataloged";}
 public static string Photometry(Pick pick){var t=pick.Target;if(t.Body.HasValue){double mag=Astronomy.Illumination(t.Body.Value,new AstroTime(pick.Best)).mag;return "Apparent magnitude "+mag.ToString("0.00")+" (model at best time)";}string text="Magnitude  V "+M(t.Vmag)+" · B "+M(t.Bmag);if(!t.Vmag.HasValue&&!t.Bmag.HasValue&&t.Magnitude.HasValue)text+=" · catalog "+M(t.Magnitude)+" (band unspecified)";return text;}
 public static string Surface(Target t){return t.SurfaceBrightness.HasValue?"Mean surface brightness (B) "+M(t.SurfaceBrightness)+" mag/arcsec²":"Surface brightness: not cataloged";}
 public static string Size(Target t){return t.Major>0?t.Major.ToString("0.#")+"′ × "+t.Minor.ToString("0.#")+"′":"not cataloged";}
 public static string Description(Target t){if(t.Body.HasValue){switch(t.Body.Value){case Body.Moon:return "Earth's natural satellite. Craters, mountain rims and dark lunar plains offer changing detail along the boundary between day and night.";case Body.Jupiter:return "A gas giant with bright cloud zones, darker belts and four prominent Galilean moons. Short videos help preserve detail through atmospheric turbulence.";case Body.Saturn:return "A gas giant surrounded by icy rings. The ring angle and the planet's apparent size change with viewing geometry.";case Body.Mars:return "A rocky planet with polar caps and dark surface markings. Its small apparent disc makes sharp focus and steady seeing especially useful.";case Body.Venus:return "A bright, cloud-covered planet whose phases change as it orbits the Sun. Its surface is hidden by thick clouds.";}}
 string constellation=Astronomy.Constellation(t.Ra,t.Dec).Name;var types=new Dictionary<string,string>{{"Open cluster","A loose grouping of stars formed together; individual stars are usually the main imaging feature."},{"Globular cluster","A dense, roughly spherical star cluster; short test frames help protect its bright central stars."},{"Galaxy","A distant system of stars, gas and dust. Faint outer structure usually needs more total integration than its bright core."},{"Emission nebula","Glowing ionized gas. An appropriate emission-line filter can improve contrast against light pollution."},{"Planetary nebula","Gas expelled by an aging star and illuminated by its hot remnant; the name does not imply a connection to planets."},{"Reflection nebula","Dust scattering the light of nearby stars. Broadband capture and darker skies help preserve faint dust detail."},{"Dark nebula","A cloud of dust silhouetted against stars or glowing gas; dark skies help reveal its low-contrast outline."},{"Supernova remnant","Expanding material left by a stellar explosion. Filaments can be faint despite the region's large size."},{"Cluster and nebula","A star cluster associated with nebulosity; protect bright stars while accumulating faint surrounding gas."}};string explanation=types.ContainsKey(t.Type)?types[t.Type]:"Use the catalog classification and angular size to plan the framing; inspect test frames for faint structure.";return t.Type+" in "+constellation+". "+explanation;}
 public static List<AltitudePoint> Track(Pick pick,Night night){var result=new List<AltitudePoint>();if(night.Dark.Count==0)return result;var start=night.Dark.First();var end=night.Dark.Last();var times=new[]{start,start.AddTicks((pick.Best-start).Ticks/2),pick.Best,pick.Best.AddTicks((end-pick.Best).Ticks/2),end}.Distinct().OrderBy(t=>t);foreach(var time in times){var eq=night.Coords(pick.Target,time);var h=Astronomy.Horizon(new AstroTime(time),night.Obs,eq.ra,eq.dec,Refraction.Normal);result.Add(new AltitudePoint{Utc=time,Alt=h.altitude,Az=h.azimuth,Label=time==pick.Best?"Best":time==start?"Dark starts":time==end?"Dark ends":""});}return result;}
 public static string Compass(double az){string[] names={"N","NE","E","SE","S","SW","W","NW"};return names[((int)Math.Round(az/45)%8+8)%8];}
 public static string Full(Pick pick,Night night){var t=pick.Target;var eq=night.Coords(t,pick.Best);var h=Astronomy.Horizon(new AstroTime(pick.Best),night.Obs,eq.ra,eq.dec,Refraction.Normal);return t.Name+"\n\n"+Description(t)+"\n\n"+Coordinates(pick,night)+"\nAt best: altitude "+h.altitude.ToString("0.0")+"° · azimuth "+h.azimuth.ToString("0.0")+"° "+Compass(h.azimuth)+"\nBest time: "+night.Time(pick.Best)+"\nAngular size: "+(t.Body.HasValue?"varies with distance; catalog thumbnail is a reference":Size(t))+"\n\n"+Photometry(pick)+(t.Body.HasValue?"":"\nNear-infrared magnitude: J "+M(t.Jmag)+" · H "+M(t.Hmag)+" · K "+M(t.Kmag)+"\n"+Surface(t))+"\nLower magnitudes mean brighter objects. Total magnitude is not surface brightness.\n\n"+(string.IsNullOrEmpty(t.Morphology)?"":"Galaxy morphology: "+t.Morphology+"\n")+(string.IsNullOrEmpty(t.CatalogNotes)?"":"Catalog note: "+t.CatalogNotes+"\n")+"\nData: "+(t.Body.HasValue?"Astronomy Engine positions / magnitude model; NASA body overview.":"Selected "+t.CatalogName+" catalog. OpenNGC coordinates are J2000; B surface brightness is the mean within its 25-mag isophote. Missing measurements remain unfilled.")+"\nImage: "+ObjectImages.Source(t)+"\nStar map: XHIP stars and constellation data from d3-celestial / Olaf Frohn, BSD-3-Clause. J2000 locator; north up, east left. StarCatalog contains credits and license.\nReference pictures do not predict your camera's framing or tonight's phase.";}
}
class ObjectPhoto:Control {
 public event Action ImageLoaded;public bool HasImage {get{return photo!=null;}}public string StatusText {get{return status;}}Image photo;Target target;bool online,loading;int attempts;System.Windows.Forms.Timer retry=new System.Windows.Forms.Timer{Interval=20000};string status="Loading color reference image…";public ObjectPhoto(Target t,bool allowOnline){target=t;online=allowOnline;DoubleBuffered=true;Cursor=Cursors.Default;AccessibleName="Object reference picture";AccessibleDescription="Object reference image";retry.Tick+=async(a,b)=>{retry.Stop();await LoadPhoto(true);};Click+=async(a,b)=>{if(photo==null&&online&&!loading){attempts=0;await LoadPhoto(true);}};Disposed+=(a,b)=>{retry.Stop();retry.Dispose();photo?.Dispose();};}
 protected override async void OnHandleCreated(EventArgs e){base.OnHandleCreated(e);await LoadPhoto(false);}
 async Task LoadPhoto(bool forceRetry){if(loading||IsDisposed)return;loading=true;attempts++;Cursor=Cursors.Default;status="Loading color reference image…";Invalidate();string path=null;try{var request=ObjectImages.Get(target,online,forceRetry);if(await Task.WhenAny(request,Task.Delay(40000)).ConfigureAwait(false)==request)path=await request.ConfigureAwait(false);}catch{}if(IsDisposed)return;Action apply=()=>{if(IsDisposed)return;try{if(path!=null)try{using(var loaded=Image.FromFile(path)){var replacement=new Bitmap(loaded);photo?.Dispose();photo=replacement;}}catch{ObjectImages.ReportReadError(target);photo=null;}if(photo==null){status=(online?ObjectImages.ErrorFor(target):"Reference image not cached.")+(online&&attempts<3?"\nRetrying automatically… Click to retry now.":online?"\nClick to retry image.":"\nConnect to load the survey picture.");Cursor=online?Cursors.Hand:Cursors.Default;if(online&&attempts<3)retry.Start();}else {retry.Stop();ImageLoaded?.Invoke();}}finally{loading=false;Invalidate();}};try{if(InvokeRequired)BeginInvoke(apply);else apply();}catch(InvalidOperationException){loading=false;}}
 protected override void OnPaint(PaintEventArgs e){e.Graphics.Clear(Style.Card);if(photo==null){TextRenderer.DrawText(e.Graphics,status,Font,ClientRectangle,Style.Muted,TextFormatFlags.HorizontalCenter|TextFormatFlags.VerticalCenter|TextFormatFlags.WordBreak);return;}double scale=Math.Min(Width/(double)photo.Width,Height/(double)photo.Height);e.Graphics.InterpolationMode=System.Drawing.Drawing2D.InterpolationMode.HighQualityBicubic;var rect=new Rectangle((Width-(int)(photo.Width*scale))/2,(Height-(int)(photo.Height*scale))/2,(int)(photo.Width*scale),(int)(photo.Height*scale));using(var attributes=new ImageAttributes()){if(Style.Theme=="Night")attributes.SetColorMatrix(new ColorMatrix(new[]{new float[]{.3f,0,0,0,0},new float[]{.59f,0,0,0,0},new float[]{.11f,0,0,0,0},new float[]{0,0,0,1,0},new float[]{0,0,0,0,1}}));e.Graphics.DrawImage(photo,rect,0,0,photo.Width,photo.Height,GraphicsUnit.Pixel,attributes);}}
}
static class ObjectView {
 public static Control Create(Pick pick,Night night,Rig rig,Form owner,bool online){var t=pick.Target;var guide=pick.Guide;var card=Style.Grid(1,34,-100);card.Tag="object-card";card.BackColor=Style.Card;card.Padding=new Padding(10,5,10,8);card.Margin=new Padding(3);var header=Style.Grid(guide.Beginner?2:1,-100);header.Controls.Add(Style.Label(t.Name,15,true),0,0);if(guide.Beginner){header.ColumnStyles[0].Width=100;header.ColumnStyles[1].SizeType=SizeType.Absolute;header.ColumnStyles[1].Width=150;header.Controls.Add(new DifficultyBadge{Dock=DockStyle.Fill,Margin=new Padding(3),Tag="beginner-badge"},1,0);}card.Controls.Add(header,0,0);
 var columns=Style.Grid(3,-100);columns.ColumnStyles[0].Width=24;columns.ColumnStyles[1].Width=49;columns.ColumnStyles[2].Width=27;var left=Style.Grid(1,24,110,-100,32);left.Padding=new Padding(0,0,12,0);left.Controls.Add(Style.Label("Why tonight",11,true),0,0);string reason="Best altitude  "+pick.Alt.ToString("0")+"° at "+night.S.Local(pick.Best).ToString("h:mm tt")+"\nImaging window  "+(pick.End-pick.Start).TotalHours.ToString("0.#")+" hours\n"+pick.Fit+"\n"+guide.Sky+"\n"+(t.Body==Body.Moon?"Lunar detail: use short video": "Moon separation  "+pick.Separation.ToString("0")+"°");var why=Style.Label(reason,9.5f);why.TextAlign=ContentAlignment.TopLeft;left.Controls.Add(why,0,1);var reference=new ObjectPhoto(t,online){Dock=DockStyle.Fill,Font=new Font("Segoe UI",9)};var caption=Style.Label(ObjectImages.Caption(t),8.5f);reference.ImageLoaded+=()=>{if(!caption.IsDisposed)caption.Text=ObjectImages.Caption(t);};left.Controls.Add(reference,0,2);left.Controls.Add(caption,0,3);columns.Controls.Add(left,0,0);
 var center=Style.Grid(1,-75,43,-25,73,34);center.Padding=new Padding(8,0,12,0);center.Controls.Add(new AltitudeChart(pick,night){Dock=DockStyle.Fill,AccessibleName="Altitude trajectory",Tag="altitude-chart"},0,0);var stats=Style.Grid(3,-100);DateTime[] times={night.Dark.FirstOrDefault(),pick.Best,night.Dark.LastOrDefault()};string[] names={"Dark starts","Best altitude","Dark ends"};for(int i=0;i<3;i++){var point=Style.Label(names[i]+"\n"+night.S.Local(times[i]).ToString("h:mm tt")+" · "+night.Altitude(t,times[i]).ToString("0")+"°",9);point.Tag="altitude-sample";stats.Controls.Add(point,i,0);}center.Controls.Add(stats,0,1);var description=Style.Label(ObjectInfo.Description(t),10);description.TextAlign=ContentAlignment.TopLeft;description.Padding=new Padding(0,6,0,0);center.Controls.Add(description,0,2);string sub=guide.SubSeconds.HasValue?guide.SubSeconds.Value.ToString("0.#")+" s":guide.Exposure;var plan=Style.Label("Capture plan\nExposure  "+sub+" · Gain  "+EquipmentLibrary.Gain(rig,true)+"\nGoal  "+guide.Integration+"\nWindow  "+night.Time(pick.Start)+" – "+night.Time(pick.End),9.5f);plan.TextAlign=ContentAlignment.TopLeft;center.Controls.Add(plan,0,3);var actions=Style.Grid(1,-100);actions.Controls.Add(Style.Button("Capture plan",(a,b)=>CaptureUI.Show(guide,owner)),0,0);center.Controls.Add(actions,0,4);columns.Controls.Add(center,1,0);
 var right=Style.Grid(1,25,60,25,120,-100);right.Padding=new Padding(10,0,0,0);right.Controls.Add(Style.Label("Coordinates",11,true),0,0);var eq=t.Body.HasValue?night.Coords(t,pick.Best):default(CosineKitty.Equatorial);var coordinates=Style.Label("RA  "+ObjectInfo.RA(t.Body.HasValue?eq.ra:t.Ra)+"\nDec "+ObjectInfo.Dec(t.Body.HasValue?eq.dec:t.Dec)+"\n"+(t.Body.HasValue?"Of date · at best time":"J2000 · catalog position"),10);coordinates.TextAlign=ContentAlignment.TopLeft;right.Controls.Add(coordinates,0,1);right.Controls.Add(Style.Label("Photometry",11,true),0,2);string data=ObjectInfo.Photometry(pick)+"\n"+(t.Body.HasValue?"Brightness is a model estimate.":(t.SurfaceBrightness.HasValue?"B surface: "+t.SurfaceBrightness.Value.ToString("0.00")+" mag/arcsec²":"Surface brightness: not cataloged")+"\nAngular size  "+ObjectInfo.Size(t)+"\n"+(!t.Jmag.HasValue&&!t.Hmag.HasValue&&!t.Kmag.HasValue?"J/H/K: not cataloged":"J "+Value(t.Jmag)+" · H "+Value(t.Hmag)+" · K "+Value(t.Kmag)))+"\nLower magnitude means brighter.";var facts=Style.Label(data,9.2f);facts.Tag="object-facts";facts.TextAlign=ContentAlignment.TopLeft;right.Controls.Add(facts,0,3);right.Controls.Add(new SkyMap(pick,night){Dock=DockStyle.Fill,AccessibleName="Sky map centered on target"},0,4);columns.Controls.Add(right,2,0);card.Controls.Add(columns,0,1);return card;
 }
 static string Value(double? number){return number.HasValue?number.Value.ToString("0.0"):"—";}
 public static void ShowData(Pick pick,Night night,Form owner){using(var form=new Form()){Style.Form(form);form.Text="Object data and sources";Style.FitScreen(form,900,640);var root=Style.Grid(1,-100,38);root.Padding=new Padding(14);var text=new TextBox{Multiline=true,ReadOnly=true,Dock=DockStyle.Fill,BorderStyle=BorderStyle.None,ScrollBars=ScrollBars.Vertical,BackColor=Style.Card,ForeColor=Style.Text,Font=new Font("Segoe UI",10),Text=ObjectInfo.Full(pick,night).Replace("\n",Environment.NewLine)};root.Controls.Add(text,0,0);root.Controls.Add(Style.Button("Close",(a,b)=>form.Close()),0,1);form.Controls.Add(root);form.ShowDialog(owner);}}
}
